.TH TURNKEY-USHAHIDI-LARAVEL-UPDATE 8 "August 2026" "TurnKey Linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
turnkey-ushahidi-laravel-update \- verify, update, or roll back Ushahidi's Laravel 8 runtime
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B turnkey-ushahidi-laravel-update --check
.br
.B turnkey-ushahidi-laravel-update --apply --dry-run
.br
.B turnkey-ushahidi-laravel-update --apply
.br
.B turnkey-ushahidi-laravel-update --rollback
.SH DESCRIPTION
The command maintains the Laravel framework embedded in the Ushahidi appliance.
It fetches only the official 8.x branch and v8.* tags from
https://github.com/laravel/framework.git. Only stable, non-prerelease tags are
eligible.
.PP
A candidate must descend from the installed commit and the CVE-2024-52301
baseline commit, be an ancestor of the official 8.x branch, declare the
laravel/framework package, match its tag version, and retain the installed
dependency and autoload contract. A downgrade, changed tag, unrelated history,
prerelease, other major version, or package-contract change fails closed.
.PP
The complete Git repository is stored at
/usr/local/share/turnkey-ushahidi/laravel-framework.git. Runtime generations
and their integrity records are stored under
/var/lib/turnkey-ushahidi/laravel. The framework and its Composer lock and
installed metadata all resolve through one current-generation link. Apply
stages and verifies an immutable Git checkout before replacing that link.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --check
Fetch and verify the official channel, validate the installed generation, and
report the newest acceptable stable tag without changing the runtime.
.TP
.B --apply --dry-run
Perform the same verification and report the proposed action without staging
or activating a generation.
.TP
.B --apply
Stage the candidate and its coherent Composer metadata, lint focused changed
PHP files, activate it, and run the Ushahidi Laravel health check. A failed
post-activation check automatically restores the prior generation.
.TP
.B --rollback
Exchange the current and previous verified generations and run the health
check. If rollback health validation fails, the original generation is
restored. Root privileges are required for apply and rollback.
.SH RECOVERY
Run --check after any interrupted operation. If a successful update later
shows an application regression, run --rollback. Do not git pull into
/var/www/ushahidi or edit the managed links. Preserve the Git repository,
/var/lib/turnkey-ushahidi/laravel, and the Ushahidi database/storage in normal
backups. If neither verified generation is healthy, leave the failing update
unapplied and obtain a reviewed TurnKey package update.
.SH SECURITY MODEL
Laravel 8 is beyond its formal guaranteed-support window. The official 8.x Git
repository is used as a best-effort source because upstream has published
post-EOL security fixes. There is no SLA or guarantee that all vulnerabilities
will be fixed. If acceptable stable tags stop, the updater intentionally stops;
it never substitutes branch HEAD, a prerelease, or an unverified fork.
.SH SEE ALSO
turnkey-ushahidi-update(8), git(1)
